course: dictionary
lesson: 3853
title: Fountain: water, drinks and ideas
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives three for fountain, so read the words around it to find the right one. «Coins thrown into a wishing fountain are usually collected for charity.» A wishing fountain is a pool of water in a park or square, because coins are thrown into the water.
explain: «Drop Mentos into a bottle of diet cola and a fountain shoots up.» The words shoots up tell you a fountain is a stream of water pushed high into the air. Ask yourself: which meaning fits? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: «She has a fountain of ideas.» Here fountain is not about water at all. It means a rich source of something, in this case ideas. Context clues help you find the right meaning even when the word looks familiar.
fact: A fountain is a stream of water pushed up into the air, often as a decoration in a park or square.
fact: A drinking fountain gives a small stream of water for you to drink from. In Australia it is often called a bubbler.
fact: A fountain can also mean a flow or rich source of something, as in «a fountain of ideas».
fact: Phrases you may meet include «water fountain», «fountain pen» and «chocolate fountain».
fact: «Refill fountains» push mains water through a filter and a cooler, and in many countries tap water is tested more often than bottled water.
exercise: «Coins thrown into a wishing fountain are usually collected for charity.» What is a wishing fountain? | *A pool of water in a park or square | A machine that sells cola | A pen that writes with ink | A tall tree with coins hanging on it
exercise: Which meaning fits «a fountain of ideas»? | *A rich source of ideas | A stream of water pushed into the air | A tap in a school for drinking | A pen for writing
exercise: Mia says a drinking fountain is for washing her hands. What is a drinking fountain really for? | *Giving a small stream of water to drink from | Keeping fish in a pond | Splashing in as a game | Making cola fizz
test: Copy one word from «Drop Mentos into a bottle of diet cola and a fountain shoots up.» that shows the fountain goes upward. | diet | *shoots | drop | bottle
test: The school corridor has a water fountain. What is it for? | To keep fish | *To give a small stream of water to drink from | To write with ink | To make cola
exam: Which sentence uses fountain to mean a rich source? | The park has a fountain in the middle | *She had a fountain of jokes for the whole class | The water fountain is cold today | He filled his bottle at the fountain
